This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Its subject is scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh, which is not shipped to consumers.
A fixture whose subject is absent cannot run: it is permanently dormant, and a dormant
fixture in the consumer's suite is worse than no fixture, because the catalog then claims
the check is self-tested when nothing tests it there.

THIS MARKER IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT.

The exemption used to be a hand-maintained string inside validate-enforcement-map.sh
(`DIST_ONLY="enforcement-map-sites"`). Three readers needed to agree about it — install.sh
(which shipped an enumerated 14 and correctly omitted this one), preclassify.sh's
map_consumer() (which mapped *every* core/fixtures/* to tests/fixtures/ and therefore
shipped it anyway on every pull), and I8 itself. They did not agree, and the reference
consumer ended up with tests/fixtures/enforcement-map-sites/ on disk with no subject script
beside it — precisely the failure this fixture exists to warn about, committed by the
mechanism that warns about it.

So the exemption now lives HERE, next to the thing it exempts, and all three readers derive
it. A list two writers must remember to update is the bug. Derive it.
